THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================

PyMuPDF and MuPDF
-----------------
    Copyright (C) Artifex Software, Inc.
    GNU Affero General Public License v3.0, or an Artifex commercial licence.
    https://pymupdf.readthedocs.io

    TSP calls PyMuPDF as a library. Two consequences worth knowing about:

    1. Handing someone a build. A PyInstaller folder or a zip of dist/TSP
       contains PyMuPDF, so the recipient is entitled to the corresponding
       source of that AGPL component. Pointing them at this repository and at
       https://pypi.org/project/pymupdf/ satisfies it.

    2. Running it as a network service. AGPL section 13 reaches users who
       interact with a modified version over a network. A server-side
       deployment triggers it. The GitHub Pages build runs PyMuPDF inside the
       visitor's own browser, which is a weaker case, and publishing the
       source at the same origin settles it either way. See docs/BROWSER.md.

    Buying an Artifex commercial licence removes both obligations. Contact
    Artifex if a client needs TSP inside a proprietary product.

